      "content": "hey i was walking past the server rack in the basement today and i could actually hear it... not just the fans but like a rhythmic pulsing in the air. it felt like staccato bursts, kind of like a syncopated beat but it was definitely coming from the wifi signal area. it went something like: long-short-short-long.... pause... then three quick micro-bursts. it felt intentional, like a sequence. can you help me figure out what kind of packet architecture would make a signal pulse in that specific rhythm? i need to know if it’s a standard handshake or something else.",
